-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hierarchical generalized linear models (with discussion)</article-title><source>J. R. Statist. Soc. <italic>B</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>619</fpage><lpage>678</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b19"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lillard</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Simultaneous equations for hazards: marriage duration and fertility timing</article-title><source>J. Econometr.</source><year>1993</year><volume>56</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>217</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubin</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>YN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parameter expansion to accelerate EM: the PX-EM algorithm</article-title><source>Biometrika</source><year>1998</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>755</fpage><lpage>770</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b21"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>YN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parameter expansion for data augmentation</article-title><source>J. Am. Statist. Ass.</source><year>1999</year><volume>94</volume><fpage>1264</fpage><lpage>1274</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b22"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>ESW</given-names></name><name><surname>Carpenter</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldstein</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Rasbash</surna